                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi BRST
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  s'
                  \\;=\;
                  \\left\{ -\mathbf{L}' + \mathbf{L}'_{BRST}, - \right\}
          %p
            The corresponding global BV-BRST differential on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+polynomial+observables"} regular polynomial observables
            is (
            %a{:href => "A+first+idea+of+quantum+field+theory#ComplexBVBRSTGlobal"}> this def.
            )
